  "title": "The model catalog grew beyond images and text",
  "summary": "The API grew a third dimension while community models, app authorization, media requests, and billing became more usable.\n\n3D generation joined the API: Trellis 2 turns images into GLB files, while Rodin 2.5 accepts images or text. Requests can return a result directly or run as asynchronous jobs. The catalog also added paid-only NanoBanana 2 Lite and Claude Sonnet 5; Claude Fable 5 returned with image input, tools, and a 1 million-token context.\n\nEligible owners can register and test OpenAI-compatible endpoints in Enter, then manage them through the dashboard, API, or Polli. Published models appear in listings and support chat, text, and streaming requests. Public IDs now use `{username}/{model-id}`, with older IDs kept as aliases; the Earnings view separates community-model rewards from app-markup earnings.\n\nGPT Image 2 now accepts dimensions within its supported bounds instead of snapping to three presets, allows larger input images, and passes through requested quality settings. NanoBanana reference-image requests no longer acquire an unwanted blank image. The week also brought fixes for GPT Image routing, WAV responses, video-model discovery, and several text-provider request errors. A model-health endpoint exposes raw status data with a selectable lookback window.\n\nApps gained an OAuth authorization-code flow with PKCE, so sign-in need not put an API key in the callback. A read-only API and Polli commands now show completed Quests and rewards. The app-directory sync was also changed to avoid a brief empty listing that could interfere with App Listed quest claims.",
